Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day. By 4 October the desk had
**412 reports** (the export repeats 15 rows; counted once by id). They were merged into #4471 as
one parser bug. They are three problems.

<Callout>
Not one issue. #4471 holds three problems, and only the first is the parser.
</Callout>

## The three problems

| # | Problem | Reports | Status |
|---|---------|--------:|--------|
| 1 | The shared parser reads dates month first; day-first tenants get flipped dates | 374 | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| 2 | The booking-v3 form hint prints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants (copper.studio, alder.physio, pale.harbour) | 33 | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |
| 3 | Dates move by one day (time zone or DST, not a month flip) | 5 | open: no ticket of its own until now |

374 + 33 + 5 = 412. The cause table below files problem 3's five reports under `parser` because
it sorts by tenant, so it shows 379 there. Intake tagged 23 of the `parser` group as `hint` and 15 of
the `hint` group as `parser`: the tag is a guess, the tenant is the evidence.

